# G-07 [PENDING SC5.2] commitReservation parses single item only
# G-08 [✔ FIXED SC2.4] Multi-item Redis overwrite (fixed but with bugs — see below)
# G-09 [DEFERRED] BasketPage.tsx 'SUCCESS' state reference (renders null, not crashing)
# G-10 [✔ FIXED SC3.1] CardElement → PaymentElement
# G-11 [PENDING SC5.1] headers() non-async in Next.js 15
# G-12 [PENDING SC4] Fake setTimeout success page
# G-13 [PENDING SC5.4] Duplicate webhook routes

# —— NEW GAPS (v2 — found in implemented code) ——
# G-NEW-01 [⚠ CRITICAL | PENDING SC2A.1] Redis product_stock empty by default
#   sync-stock-to-redis.mjs has 3 hardcoded test IDs — real products not in Redis
#   Every checkout fails with INSUFFICIENT_STOCK (confirmed: checkpoint 2.A incomplete)
#   Fix: Sanity fallback seeds Redis on cold miss using already-fetched products[]

# G-NEW-02 [⚠ CRITICAL | PENDING SC2A.1] Reservation stored BEFORE decrement loop
#   Item 1 decremented, item 2 fails → rollbackReservation reads JSON with item 2
#   Item 2 was never decremented → restoring it over-credits Redis by item 2 quantity
#   Fix: Track reserved[] inline, store reservation AFTER all decrements succeed

# G-NEW-03 [⚠ CRITICAL | PENDING SC2A.2] rollbackReservation splits(':') on JSON array
#   reserveStock.ts:284 — produces garbage Redis key (e.g. '[{"productId"')
#   No stock restored on any failure path → Redis stock permanently incorrect after failure
#   Fix: Parse JSON with legacy fallback, restore ALL items in array

# G-NEW-04 [⚠ CRITICAL | PENDING SC3A.1] amountPln display formula 100x wrong
#   SC2.2 stores amountPln = totalAmount / 100 (PLN, e.g. 999.00)
#   SC3.1 implemented (amountPln / 100).toFixed(2) → 9.99 PLN instead of 999.00 PLN
#   Fix: amountPln.toFixed(2) PLN (already in PLN, no division needed)

# G-NEW-05 [⚠ HIGH | PENDING SC3A.2] Success page accessible without payment
#   router.push('/checkout/success') has no PI ID → Case B bypasses payment verification
#   Any user navigating to /checkout/success directly sees "Order Confirmed" + basket cleared
#   Fix: router.push('/checkout/success?payment_intent=${paymentIntent.id}') → always verify

# G-NEW-06 [⚠ CRITICAL | PENDING SC5.3] releaseReservation splits(':') on JSON array
#   route.ts:83 — same corruption bug as G-NEW-03 but in webhook
#   payment_intent.payment_failed → corrupt Redis key, stock never restored
#   Fix: Parse JSON with legacy fallback, restore ALL items

